---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyCommand from '../components/copyCommand';
import { installCommand, releasesUrl } from '../lib/nav';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

// Every terminal transcript on this page was captured from lattice 1.0.0-beta-2
// running against a two-package repo. Re-capture them rather than editing by hand.
const initOutput = `✓ wrote lattice.json
✓ wrote .lattice/schema.json
✓ updated .gitignore

next: lattice run build`;

const config = `{
  "$schema": ".lattice/schema.json",
  "latticeVersion": "1.0.0-beta-2",
  "workspaces": [
    { "name": "ui",  "path": "packages/ui" },
    { "name": "web", "path": "apps/web", "dependsOn": ["ui"] }
  ],
  "tasks": {
    "build": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": ["src/**/*"],
      "outputs": ["dist/**"]
    }
  }
}`;

const setupOutput = `❖ lattice  setup
● ui npm install
● web npm install
❖ setup complete`;

const coldRun = `lattice: running \`build\` across 2 workspaces
lattice: ui:build: hash 664f4cd394564ff5
lattice: ui:build: cache miss (nothing cached for this task yet)
ui:build: running
ui:build: done (0.21s)
lattice: web:build: hash d97c6e8a847a1e0f
lattice: web:build: cache miss (nothing cached for this task yet)
web:build: running
web:build: done (0.18s)
lattice: 2 tasks, 0 cached, 0 failed, 0.39s`;

const warmRun = `lattice: running \`build\` across 2 workspaces
lattice: ui:build: hash 664f4cd394564ff5
ui:build: cache hit [664f4cd3]
lattice: web:build: hash d97c6e8a847a1e0f
web:build: cache hit [d97c6e8a]
lattice: 2 tasks, 2 cached, 0 failed, 0.00s
lattice: full cache, nothing to run`;

const windowsInstallCommand = 'irm https://latticeandcompany.github.io/lattice/install.ps1 | iex';

const next = [
	{
		name: 'Installation',
		href: withBase('/docs/installation'),
		blurb: 'Supported platforms, building from source, shell completions, and how to remove it.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Workspaces',
		href: withBase('/docs/workspaces'),
		blurb: 'What a workspace is, how to declare its path and dependencies, and how a task resolves inside one.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Caching',
		href: withBase('/docs/caching'),
		blurb: 'What goes into a task hash, and what makes a cached result valid to restore.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Toolchains',
		href: withBase('/docs/toolchains'),
		blurb: 'Pin the version of node, rust, go, or any other tool your repo builds against.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Get started · Lattice"
	description="Install Lattice in a repo, write a lattice.json, and run a task that comes back from cache the second time."
>
	<section class="px-3 pt-5 pb-4">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h1 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.03em;">
				Get started
			</h1>
			<p class="fs-5 mb-0" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
				Six steps from a repo with no Lattice in it to a build that comes back from cache the second time
				you run it. You need a terminal and the tools your workspaces already use.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<ol class="steps mx-auto list-unstyled mb-0" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Install it into your repo</h2>
					<p>From the root of the repo you want to use Lattice in:</p>
					<CopyCommand client:visible command={installCommand} />
					<p class="mt-3">
						The script picks the archive for your platform, checks its SHA-256 against the release's
						published checksums, and refuses to install on a mismatch. The binary lands in
						<code>.lattice/bin/</code>, and the script adds that path to your <code>.gitignore</code> if
						the repo already has one. The only thing it writes outside the repo is a <code>PATH</code>
						line in your shell config. To skip that line, pass <code>--no-modify-path</code> and call
						<code>./.lattice/bin/lattice</code> directly.
					</p>
					<p>
						That script covers macOS, Linux, and Windows under Git Bash. In PowerShell, run the
						Windows installer instead:
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>{windowsInstallCommand}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						It writes the same <code>.lattice\bin</code> and adds that directory to your user
						<code>PATH</code>, asking first. Every published build is listed on the
						<a href={releasesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">releases page</a>. See
						<a href={withBase('/docs/installation')}>Installation</a> for the switches both
						installers take.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Check that it runs</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice --version</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>lattice 1.0.0-beta-2</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						If your shell can't find <code>lattice</code>, open a new terminal so the
						<code>PATH</code> line takes effect.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Scaffold a config</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice init</code></pre>
					<p>
						On a terminal, <code>init</code> scans the repo first, then asks you to confirm the
						workspaces and the pinned tool versions it found. If the scan finds nothing, it walks you
						through adding them one at a time. To write what the scan finds without being asked, add
						<code>-y</code>.
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{initOutput}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						<code>lattice.json</code> is your config. Commit <code>.lattice/schema.json</code> too, so
						your editor validates that config as you type. <code>init</code> gitignores the rest:
						<code>.lattice/cache/</code>, <code>.lattice/toolchains/</code>, and
						<code>.lattice/bin/</code> are all per-machine.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Declare your workspaces</h2>
					<p>
						A workspace is a directory with its own manifest. It is the unit Lattice runs and caches
						tasks in. List each one by literal path, and say which ones depend on which:
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--file"><code>{config}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						Each workspace runs the tool already in its directory, identified from that directory's
						lockfile or manifest. <code>^build</code> means the <code>build</code> task of every
						workspace this one depends on, run first. <code>inputs</code> are the files the cache
						watches for changes, and <code>outputs</code> are the files it captures and restores. To
						write a command yourself instead, set <code>"auto": false</code> on the workspace and give
						it a <code>scripts</code> map.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Install dependencies</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice setup</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{setupOutput}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						<code>setup</code> installs any tool versions you pinned, then installs each workspace's own
						dependencies. Run it as often as you like. Lattice skips a workspace whose lockfile hasn't
						changed.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Run a task</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice run build -l</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{coldRun}</code></pre>
					<p>
						<code>ui</code> builds before <code>web</code> because <code>web</code> depends on it.
						Workspaces with no dependency between them run at the same time. <code>-l</code> is short
						for <code>--loquacious</code>, and it prints this plain log. Without it, on a terminal, you
						get a live display instead.
					</p>
					<p>Run it again without changing a file:</p>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{warmRun}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						Same hashes, so nothing re-ran. <code>dist/</code> came back out of
						<code>.lattice/cache/</code>. Edit a file under <code>src/</code> and that workspace's hash
						changes. That workspace builds again, and so does anything that depends on it. Everything
						else still comes from cache.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h2 class="fw-bold mb-4" style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
				Where to go next
			</h2>
			<div class="row g-3">
				{
					next.map((item) => (
						<div class="col-12 col-sm-6">
							<a href={item.href} class="card h-100 text-decoration-none next-card">
								<div class="card-body p-4">
									<span class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 fw-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--text);">
										{item.name}
										<i class="bi bi-arrow-right next-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true" />
									</span>
									<span class="d-block mb-0" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.6;">
										{item.blurb}
									</span>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.steps {
		counter-reset: step;
	}
	.step {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
		column-gap: 1.25rem;
		padding-bottom: 3rem;
	}
	.step:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
	}
	/* The rail runs through the number and down to the next step, so the sequence
	   reads as one thread rather than six detached blocks. */
	.step__num {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2.5rem;
		height: 2.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--surface);
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--focus);
	}
	.step:not(:last-child) .step__num::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: 2.5rem;
		bottom: -3rem;
		left: 50%;
		width: 1px;
		background: var(--border-subtle);
	}
	.step__title {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
	}
	.step__body :global(p) {
		color: var(--text-subtle);
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.step__body :global(code) {
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		color: var(--text);
	}
	.step__code {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--surface-2);
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	.step__code::before {
		content: '$ ';
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	.step__code--out::before,
	.step__code--file::before {
		content: none;
	}
	.step__code--out {
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	.next-card__arrow {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		transition: transform 0.15s ease;
	}
	.next-card:hover .next-card__arrow {
		transform: translateX(0.2rem);
		color: var(--focus);
	}
	@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
		.step {
			grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
			column-gap: 0.9rem;
		}
		.step__num {
			width: 2rem;
			height: 2rem;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
		}
		.step:not(:last-child) .step__num::after {
			top: 2rem;
		}
	}
</style>
